      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "/root",
        "notes": "Reviewed complete Scope and limitations, F1–F6 and Verification 1.1–2.1 against current finite-grid/envelope theorems and published split-conformal theorem, actual regular conditional law and expectation definitions. Two-state variable X is sigma(U)-measurable, so R=X, E[R]=1/4, P(R>1/4)=1/2; no high-probability inference follows from the mean alone. Conditional guarantees require actual sectionwise exchangeable laws with every bound/nesting/endpoint hypothesis; no existence inference, independence shortcut, feature/subgroup conditioning or calibration-sample-conditional guarantee is asserted. Split conformal supplier only bounds its miscoverage event under its own training-fixed jointly measurable score/conditional exchangeability assumptions; top-label calibration is a different conditional-expectation identity. Adaptive reuse and shift outside exchangeability have no inherited guarantee; finite tail maxima dominate original losses without claiming improved actual risk. Compared CRC §1.2, §2.4, §4.1; Foundations Ch.4 intro, §4.1 and §4.3; Shafer–Vovk §3.1 permutation formulation. No AC, new mathematical defect or diagram issue; no consumer edit needed. See alpha-batch-98-3a report."
